# The Network: GitHub
#
# Expects a region group that is not Hong Kong. Must precede the general proxy classification, which would otherwise send these to the default proxy group.
#
# Measured 2026-08-12: both providers' Hong Kong exits intermittently drop the TLS handshake to GitHub's Asia frontend. Failure rates on fresh connections were 15% and 15% and 17.5% across two nodes of one provider and 12.5% on the other provider, while www.google.com through the same node at the same moment stayed at zero. Japan and Singapore were clean at 0 of 30 each.
#
# The destination is not at fault. Hong Kong and Singapore both resolve to the same frontend, 20.205.243.166, and only Hong Kong fails; Japan resolves to 20.27.177.113. So the fault is in the path from Hong Kong to that frontend, which is why changing provider does not help and changing exit region does.
#
# The failure shape at the gateway: the client hello goes into the tunnel, 320 bytes out, and nothing comes back for 7.27 seconds before the far end closes. A browser retries and succeeds, which is why this surfaces as a page that fails once and loads on reload rather than as an outage.
#
# The fault is intermittent. Hong Kong recovered on its own about half an hour later for github.com while still failing 2 of 20 on the githubusercontent hosts, so a clean spot check does not mean the pin can be removed.
#
# ghcr.io lives here rather than in Rescue/BlockedDirect.list or Library/Direct/Registries.list: it needs a proxy anyway because download classification would send it direct, and it is GitHub, so it should share their exit.
#
# formulae.brew.sh is a GitHub Pages custom domain (CNAME homebrew.github.io). Download classification sends it DIRECT, which is why it cannot stay with brew.sh and docs.brew.sh or with Library/Direct/Registries.list. Measured 2026-08-16: three fresh fetches of the 34MB formula.jws.json index each timed out at 90s after 5.8 to 8.8MB (64 to 98kB/s); the same file through Japan finished in 1.28 to 1.39s (24 to 27MB/s). The 21MB cask.jws.json index timed out the same way DIRECT and finished in 2.14s through Japan. brew.sh and docs.brew.sh already reach a proxy through CDN classification, so they stay out of this list.
#
# github.io is deliberately absent. GitHub Pages is served from different infrastructure and was not part of the github.com handshake measurement; the Pages custom domain above is pinned on its own evidence.
#
# Release assets and Copilot result blobs sit on S3 and Azure, not on the suffixes above. Unpinned they fall through to FINAL, which is the default proxy group and is often Hong Kong, the path that fails.

DOMAIN-SUFFIX,github.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,githubassets.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,githubusercontent.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,githubapp.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,githubnext.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,ghcr.io
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,formulae.brew.sh
DOMAIN,github-cloud.s3.amazonaws.com
DOMAIN-WILDCARD,github-production-*.s3.amazonaws.com
DOMAIN,copilotprodattachments.blob.core.windows.net
DOMAIN-WILDCARD,productionresultssa*.blob.core.windows.net
